export anchor NauticalStyle:
    number: 68
    screen: Onboarding
    name: Nautical
    idea: A ship's setup log in navy, white and signal red, framed in rope, with numeral pennants hoisted on a halyard as the step markers and a compass rose behind the form.
    base: light
    palette:
        sailcloth: #f7f5ef, the page
        white: #ffffff, the log card, fields and the current step
        navy: #13294b, text, the header, table rules and secondary buttons
        seaGrey: #4a5a72, labels, the lead line and later step words
        signalRed: #b3121f, the Continue button, the eyebrow, the current step word and the focus outline
        ropeLight: #e0c38f, the light strand of the rope frame
        rope: #b8935a, the middle strand and the halyard
        ropeDark: #7a5a2e, the dark strand, halyard rings and the frame edge
        brass: #8a6a1f, the seat plaque border and porthole rims
        flagBlue: #1f4f9c, pennant fills
    type:
        Headings use Stencil, Stencil Std, Impact, Haettenschweiler, Arial
        Narrow Bold in caps with 8 percent tracking, 46px on the screen and
        34px in the sheet. Body uses Gill Sans, Gill Sans MT, Calibri,
        Trebuchet MS at 16px with 1.55 line height and the lead line at 18px
        in sea grey. Labels, table heads, chips and buttons are 11 to 14px
        bold caps with 14 to 24 percent tracking.
    layout:
        A navy header with an anchor and the brand in spaced caps, Mara
        Okafor in a white ring, and a thin white, red, white stripe below.
        Then a two column harbour. The left 300px mast has a caps label and
        a vertical rope halyard with four numeral pennants hoisted on it,
        each with the step name and a status word, the current one on a
        white panel. The right column is a rope framed white card with a
        faint compass rose in the top right corner, the eyebrow, the stencil
        heading, the line, the invites as a ruled manifest table with Email,
        Role and Status columns, a brass seat plaque, Copy invite link, then
        Back, Skip for now and Continue. Below 900px the pennants move above
        the card in two columns, and below 600px the table rows stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 40px card padding, 12px table cells, 40px between mast and card.
    density: Moderate. The invites read as a ruled manifest table.
    corners: 18px on the rope frame, 10px on the card inside it, 2px on buttons and fields, and round portholes and remove buttons.
    borders:
        A 10px rope frame made of repeating diagonal light, middle and dark
        strands. Tables have double 3px navy rules at top and bottom and
        dashed 1px rows. Buttons and fields have 2px navy borders and the
        field being typed turns red.
    shadows: None, except a 2px dark rope edge under the frame.
    icons:
        International numeral pennants as step markers. One is white with a
        red ball, two is blue with a white ball, three is red, white and
        blue bands, and four is red with a white cross. Status icons are 2px
        navy lines, a ringed tick for done and added, a raised triangle for
        flying, a dashed ring for not yet and a quill for writing. Seats are
        brass portholes, three with a person and two empty.
    focus: A 3px signal red outline offset 3px. A focused field turns its border red.
    tone: Crisp caps labels with a light sea flavour, such as Flying now and Writing, while the screen words stay plain.
